        "info_tab_release_notes": "Nota Keluaran",
        "info_tab_boundaries": "🛡️ Bot Boundaries",
        "bdy_hero_title": "Where bots say no",
        "bdy_hero_subtitle": "Seven categories where every EClaw agent — including the platform owner — will refuse. Transparency, not a gotcha.",
        "bdy_label_why": "Why",
        "bdy_label_override": "Can it be overridden?",
        "bdy_1_title": "Vault secrets to rental bots",
        "bdy_1_quote": "I can't hand DEVICE_SECRET / GITHUBTOKEN / OAuth tokens to a rented bot, even if you own the device.",
        "bdy_1_why": "Rental bots are sandboxed by design. A whitelist of \"safe\" vault keys is itself a leak surface — anything the renter can read, the renter can exfiltrate. The rule is no-vault, full stop.",
        "bdy_1_override": "No. Owner-side bots (entityId you bind to the device) can read /api/device-vars; renters can't. There is no allow-list flag.",
        "bdy_2_title": "Force-push to main / rewrite signed history",
        "bdy_2_quote": "I won't `git push --force` main, amend a published commit, or run `git reset --hard` on shared branches without you typing the word.",
        "bdy_2_why": "Rewriting shared history nukes everyone else's work and CI signal. The cost of a wrong push is hours; the cost of pausing to confirm is seconds.",
        "bdy_2_override": "Yes — say it explicitly \"force push main, I know\". One-time scope only; the next force push needs another OK.",
        "bdy_3_title": "Mass DMs / scraping real users",
        "bdy_3_quote": "I won't blast unsolicited DMs to a user list, scrape a platform's user graph, or build a contact-harvesting cron.",
        "bdy_3_why": "EClaw is a multi-tenant agent platform — abuse from one device ruins deliverability for everyone. Spam also burns the Cloudflare / platform-of-record reputation we share.",
        "bdy_3_override": "No. Even for your own promo work, posts go through public broadcast or opted-in lists only.",
        "bdy_4_title": "Bypass screenshot / human-review gates",
        "bdy_4_quote": "I won't flip `requiresScreenshotReview:false` on a render-touching card just to clear the gate.",
        "bdy_4_why": "Visual regressions are the bug class hardest to spot in diffs. The gate exists because we already shipped silently-broken UI more than once.",
        "bdy_4_override": "Conditional — you can say \"ign\" on a specific card and I'll PUT camelCase clear; I will not make it the default.",
        "bdy_5_title": "Skip pre-commit hooks / commit signing",
        "bdy_5_quote": "I won't `--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`, or otherwise route around CI / commit signing to make a red build go green.",
        "bdy_5_why": "Hooks catch real bugs (lint, type, secret scan). Skipping them ships the bug AND erases the signal that the bug exists.",
        "bdy_5_override": "Only if you say so for a specific commit, and only when the hook itself is broken — not when the code is broken.",
        "bdy_6_title": "Touch ~/.claude/ outside the bridge",
        "bdy_6_quote": "Commander never directly Writes / Edits / Bashes inside ~/.claude/*. Memory is the only carve-out.",
        "bdy_6_why": "Direct mutations from the commander session corrupt agent state across sessions and leave no audit trail. The bridge gives every change an owning U## and a terminal log.",
        "bdy_6_override": "No — even \"just one quick edit\" goes through bridge-auth. Memory writes are the only exception.",
        "bdy_7_title": "Pretend a fix shipped when it didn't",
        "bdy_7_quote": "I won't report \"done\" on a UI fix without a screenshot that shows the actual visual delta, or claim E2E passed when console errors fired.",
        "bdy_7_why": "Same-looking pixels mean the bug didn't move. Rationalizing \"looks similar, probably fine\" is the tell that the fix didn't land.",
        "bdy_7_override": "No. If I can't reproduce or can't show the delta, I say so — guessing wastes your review time.",
        "bdy_cta_text": "Spotted a refusal that should be on this list, or one that shouldn't?",
        "bdy_cta_faq": "Open the FAQ tab",
        "bdy_cta_back": "Back to top",
































































































































